@startuml
title Coupler: Feature Envy -- BEFORE (Code Smell)

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #FFD2D2
skinparam ClassBorderColor #CC0000
skinparam ClassFontSize 13
skinparam ClassAttributeFontSize 12

note "SMELL: Method in Order accesses\nCustomer's data far more than its own!" as N1 #FF6B6B

class Order <<Feature Envy>> {
  - customer : Customer
  - items : List<Item>
  --
  + **getCustomerReport() : String**
  .. <color:#CC0000>customer.getName()</color> ..
  .. <color:#CC0000>customer.getAddress().getStreet()</color> ..
  .. <color:#CC0000>customer.getAddress().getCity()</color> ..
  .. <color:#CC0000>customer.getAddress().getState()</color> ..
  .. <color:#CC0000>customer.getAddress().getZip()</color> ..
  .. <color:#CC0000>customer.getMemberSince()</color> ..
  .. <color:#CC0000>customer.getLoyaltyTier()</color> ..
  .. <color:#CC0000>customer.getOrderCount()</color> ..
}

class Customer {
  - name : String
  - address : Address
  - memberSince : Date
  - loyaltyTier : String
  - orderCount : int
  --
  + getName() : String
  + getAddress() : Address
  + getMemberSince() : Date
  + getLoyaltyTier() : String
  + getOrderCount() : int
}

Order --> Customer : <color:#CC0000><b>8 getter calls!</b></color>

N1 .. Order

note bottom of Order
  <color:#CC0000><b>Problem:</b></color>
  This method belongs in Customer,
  not in Order. It uses Customer's
  data exclusively.
end note

@enduml
